{"assets":["/statement-assets/1099a507b37fe02396b9ef46ddbf04a7bdffac4b2b033a01d032420453d906fb.png","/statement-assets/62b2fdd26a3246fb497cb9f3cb83c00274f43e16f15658866fd32020eb2709cb.png","/statement-assets/bc4603da108ca630eadc282edb0ddf574ac6fda04a7098db8fd7cf105395e975.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"982","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Billiard"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider a "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billiard_table"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"billiard table"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of rectangular size $$$n \\times m$$$ with four pockets. Let's introduce a coordinate system with the origin at the lower left corner (see the picture). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/1099a507b37fe02396b9ef46ddbf04a7bdffac4b2b033a01d032420453d906fb.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is one ball at the point $$$(x, y)$$$ currently. Max comes to the table and strikes the ball. The ball starts moving along a line that is parallel to one of the axes or that makes a $$$45^{\\circ}$$$ angle with them. We will assume that: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the angles between the directions of the ball before and after a collision with a side are equal, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the ball moves indefinitely long, it only stops when it falls into a pocket, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the ball can be considered as a point, it falls into a pocket if and only if its coordinates coincide with one of the pockets, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" initially the ball is not in a pocket. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the ball can move along some side, in this case the ball will just fall into the pocket at the end of the side."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to determine whether the ball will fall into a pocket eventually, and if yes, which of the four pockets it will be."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains $$$6$$$ integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$, $$$x$$$, $$$y$$$, $$$v_x$$$, $$$v_y$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n, m \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$0 \\leq x \\leq n$$$; $$$0 \\leq y \\leq m$$$; $$$-1 \\leq v_x, v_y \\leq 1$$$; $$$(v_x, v_y) \\neq (0, 0)$$$) — the width of the table, the length of the table, the $$$x$$$-coordinate of the initial position of the ball, the $$$y$$$-coordinate of the initial position of the ball, the $$$x$$$-component of its initial speed and the $$$y$$$-component of its initial speed, respectively. It is guaranteed that the ball is not initially in a pocket."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the coordinates of the pocket the ball will fall into, or $$$-1$$$ if the ball will move indefinitely."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 3 2 2 -1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 4 2 0 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10 10 10 1 -1 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first sample: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/62b2fdd26a3246fb497cb9f3cb83c00274f43e16f15658866fd32020eb2709cb.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second sample: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/bc4603da108ca630eadc282edb0ddf574ac6fda04a7098db8fd7cf105395e975.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample the ball will never change its $$$y$$$ coordinate, so the ball will never fall into a pocket."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"982E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/982/problem/E"}